I've talked before about how there's  been a worldwide move away from the  United States dollar in the world of  currencies and in November of last year  we did a big story about this where I  explained that the dollar sort of has  this privileged position which is good  for people in the United States it's  used as a trading currency and a lot of  the world two-thirds of global reserves  are in dollars two-thirds of all  physical dollar bills are outside of the  US so the point of the story I did back  in November is that there's significant  global reliance on the dollar and that  this is good for the United States in a  few ways it helps to keep interest rates  low  it makes selling bonds easy because so  many countries around the world already  have dollars it makes our exports worth  more because there is more demand for  our currency it gives us a geopolitical  negotiating clout clout it's positive  for us in a bunch of different ways but  partially because of Donald Trump's  tariffs world countries have started to  move away from the dollar which is not  good for the United States in a number  of ways not only has the story been  growing it's actually now sort of tying  into Russia's manipulations and the  positioning of China geopolitically  because remember that the context here  is Russia's geopolitics for decades have  been to sow discord in the United States  carryout I guess we'd call them  initiatives to make people question the  stability of our democratic systems we  saw them do that with the 2016 election  create tension create conflict and  they've been doing it really really well  and what Russia is now doing  economically is shifting their financial  reserves away from the United States  dollar and towards the Chinese yuan  which will be yet another way in which  they are going to help destabilize the  United States as well as euros and some  Japanese yen what Russia did back in  April we just learned about it now or  maybe it was later in 2018 is they sold  about a hundred billion dollars in u.s.  holdings from its reserves and they  shifted that hundred billion into  Chinese yuan euros and yen this is not  just an economic  decision and economically it may not  even be that great for them in the short  run but it is part of their geopolitical  tactics and strategy and the antics that  they've become known for part of this is  well if they sell some of their US  dollars they'll be less exposed to US  sanctions against them if you don't have  as many US dollars you're less impacted  by those American sanctions but the  political aspect of this goes beyond  that because Putin said just a couple of  months ago quote we aren't ditching the  dollar the dollar is ditching us which  of course is interesting in the sense  that he is saying well there are  elements of the dollar that are not good  for us to hold it as a reserve currency  but it's all part of the geopolitical  play that Putin is doing and I have to  tell him it's sort of genius right I  mean in a way this is a multi-pronged  attack in every way  Putin has Trump and the US over a barrel  and I want to be really clear because I  know people will write in and say David  you know you're you're understating the  fact that this move could be bad for  Russia economically that's right if you  evaluate this decision that Russia's  making to get away from the dollar only  short-term economics it could actually  be bad for Russia the yields on some of  the currencies Russia's shifting to are  lower than yields on the US dollar in  the short term this might actually hurt  Russia economically to some degree but  in geopolitics that really doesn't  matter the dollars not doom the dollar  is going to be fine whether or not  Russia shifts reserves in or out  it's the clout and the positioning of  the United States that's increasingly in  question on the world stage one way in  which the dollar and our bonds could be  headed to a downgrade is if the shutdown  continues I read a couple of pieces  suggesting that our credit rating could  be downgraded if the shutdown goes on  much longer  Putin is actually the guy who is playing  the 4d chess in a way that Trump can't  conceive of I wish it weren't the truth  it doesn't make me happy  to come to you and say look at the  clever stuff Putin is doing to have the  United States and Trump over a barrel  but he's doing it and he's actually  doing it pretty well
 

